WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.168
-Our next guest is the Oscar
nominated writer and directo

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
behind films like
"The Sixth Sense,"

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.938 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"Signs," and "Split."

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:08.475
His latest film, "Old,"
is in theaters July 23rd.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.278 line:92%
-You're 11, right, Trent?

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm 6.
-No.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really.
Are you 10, 11?

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.086 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-He's not lying. He's 6.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm specifically
6 and a quarter.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She's 11.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:29.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're feeling unsafe.
There is a lot going on here

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.531 line:92%
-They're playing with us.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.766 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's leave it.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.868 line:92%
-Have you seen my children

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is everyone trying
to play a joke on us?

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:41.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What?
-Aren't these your children?

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.777 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-I'm right here, Mom.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:47.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show M. Night Shyamalan

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.684 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:55.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, buddy. Welcome back.
Good to see you.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.891 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Man. So good to be back.
-It's great to have you back

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.395 line:92%
Things are a little differen

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the last time
you were here.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, definitely.
I was -- You know,

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm always a dramaturge,
so the structure of things -

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Maybe Amy should go after me,

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.638 line:92%
because entertainment value.

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.872 line:92%
You want it to rise, you know?

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's like --
This just feels like

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.342 line:92%
it's a de-escalation somehow

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm funny, but
I'm the Amy Poehler in India

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm an Asian...
-Oh, gotcha. Oh, that's good

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:26.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if it airs abroad,
we'll flip it.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll re-edit it so that
they have that same feeling.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.292 line:92%
So, this is about an island.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
A secluded island
where people age very quickly.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's based on a graphic nove
that somebody gave you.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
As soon as you were readin
"Sandcastle,"

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.969
did you think to yourself,
"Oh, there's a film here"?

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:46.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it was given by
my daughters for Father's Day.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:49.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they're very good
at picking material for me

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:52.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has kind of
darker movements

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
and kind of philosophy
behind it.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.015 size:84% position:42%
But as I was reading --
It's a graphic novel,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:56.883 size:84% position:42% line:92%
so it's very cinematic.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:00.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Wow. This idea is amazing."

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's exactly what I'm thinking
at the time,

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
I'm the age I am, here, 50

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.461
and my kids now are adults
and my parents are older.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like --
That's all I'm thinking about,

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
is, man, everything
is moving so fast.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.133 line:92%
We talk about that a lot.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.168 size:88% position:44%
-Well, it's -- You know,
I think that it's weird

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you internally
are concerned

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have your own fear
about your own aging,

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then there's
that really scary thing

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
of just how fast
your kids grow up,

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:25.078
which is a big, you know,
thematic element of this.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:28.014
Your kids are growing up so fast
that one of your daughters

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:31.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
was the second unit director
on this film.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:31.885 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah. Both daughters --

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.319 size:84% position:42%
My oldest two daughters
worked on the movie.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.390
One is a musician and wrote th
song that's key to the movie

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the middle daughter
was the second unit director

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.562
So we're at one end of the
beach, I'm directing here,

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:43.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she's directing
at the other side.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she directs on "Servants."
So it's crazy.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'd have drinks afterward
at the end of the day

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
like work buddies
and talk about it.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you -- Are you --
Did you know going into it

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you would have a good
working relationship

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your kids
if you were on set?

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I hoped so.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.879 size:81% position:41%
-You know, our house
is very much the house

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.813 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
built on the arts.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody's always talking
about the arts

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:06.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the good and the bad
of being a professional artist

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.255
And so the relationship
has always been that way,

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of learning
about the art form.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.425 line:92%
It's worked out fantastic.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:15.628
I mean, we share similar tastes,
I think.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was
surprisingly positive.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.233 line:92%
-You did this on a beach.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it seems
like very idyllic

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a wonderful place
to shoot a film.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yet,
you were sort of overcome

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:30.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
with not just issues like COVI
affecting production,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
but a hurricane, as well?
-Yeah.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a tricky situation
to shoot in,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.150 size:84% position:42%
and we shot, obviously,
during the pandemic.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were actually one
of the first movies to go,

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.653 line:92%
if not the first movie to go

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we were making up everythin
of how to, you know,

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.558 line:92%
manage in a situation like that.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:49.062 size:84% position:42%
And we were forced into
the hurricane season

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:49.829 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of the Caribbean.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a hurricane came
and destroyed all the sets

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we rebuilt it,
and three days

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
before we shot,
we were in rehearsals,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.538 size:81% position:41%
everyone flew there,
and there is no beach.

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is completely gone.
Road had gone.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
They call me and were like
"There's no beach."

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I didn't -- I didn't kno
what was going to happen.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
I pay for these movies.
So, these are small movies

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:09.782 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This isn't Marvel.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is like a --
You know, that's all we have

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:13.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Also, who do you call
to get a new beach?

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:17.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was it. That's it.
That was our --

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, luckily, a little par
of the beach came back.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:22.328
We shot on that, and then
every day it came back.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you ever --
Do you ever think

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.331 size:88% position:44%
or did you ever think,
"This feels like a twist

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.768
in one of my movies that the
beach would just be gone"?

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.804
-Well, shooting in a pandemic --
The pandemic itself felt like --

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
People keep coming up
and saying,

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This is like something
you write."

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"No, I'm just pretending.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.112 line:92%
This is way too serious for me."

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:42.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so doing this in the middl
of that was scary.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:45.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think for us
as a crew and the actors,

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.421
it actually, you know, got u
in a certain place, I think.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:51.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when you see the movie,
I think a lot of the energ

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.526 line:92%
you felt there is very specifi

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
to that time period
of our lives.

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You, of course,
make these thrillers

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:59.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are incredibly iconic
that play

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
with our fears
and our insecurities.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some might think
that you are a man

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
without fear,
based on the subject matter.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you yourself --
For example,

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
you would not like
a turbulent flight.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no.
I'm scared of a lot of things.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as a kid,
I was scared of everything

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
My parents would always
have to make,

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:15.982 line:92%
you know, precautions of, like

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't leave him alone,"
and this and that.

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:19.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
"He's scared of this sound
and scared of this."

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
And flights.
Just scared of everything.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:25.258
I think -- I make these movies
I think to work through this

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:29.862
so I can be somewhat courageou
in the presence of other men

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.664 line:92%
So, you know, just act normal.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:32.899 line:92%
-Another thing that I wonder

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:37.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does it take an inner courag
to act in your films?

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:41.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you have a cameo
in all of your films.

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's something
that I always enjoy.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:46.245
Is that something --
Do you get anxiety before you go

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
and perform in a scene
that you also have to direct

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean, it's a
different part of my brain

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.353 line:92%
but this is how I handle it.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:56.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
I give myself
unlimited amount of takes.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:59.659 line:92%
So my takes, I do like 30, 40,

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:02.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
however many amount of takes
I need to do.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll take it
just to get one take

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has any kind of voracit
that's good,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.802 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and so I try not to let

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
the other actors see
how many takes I give myself

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.173 size:75% position:38%
-Right, because then
they would want 50?

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-Do you -- Have you found

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the years,
when you look at your 50 takes

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:18.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
have you found like,
"You know what?

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:20.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
My earlier takes were better
and I made a mistake."

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or do you really feel like
"I warmed up into it."

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no. It has to --
It's almost, like, random.

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:26.552 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It has to be by chance.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:29.655
So I do 50 takes, and, like, 3
is the take that you guys see.

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just have to
kind of move through it.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:32.658 line:92%
There's no skill involved.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.827 size:84% position:42%
It's just, you know,
trying different colors

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then,
"Wow. That felt right."

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:39.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- Another sort of thread
that I feel like runs

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
through a lot of your film
is Pennsylvania's Philadelphia

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.171 line:92%
And I always think that's nice

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's obviously
where you're from,

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you like to give it
a shout-out.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, "Well, this i
obviously not going to be

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
a part of this movie
that takes place on the beach.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, like, right --
Early on, somebody --

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:55.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"we're from Philadelphia."

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that something
that you really --

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's important
for you to get in?

00:06:58.551 --> 00:06:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. You know,
that's where I'm from.

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:02.155
I think, you know, the audiences
around the world

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:05.191 size:88% position:44%
kind of look for that --
kind of it's from there.

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some authors
always make movies

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.494 line:92%
about the place that they're in.

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:12.265
And this was one I guess based
on my feelings about vacatio

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:14.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
and things like that when
the family goes on vacation.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.002 line:92%
I'm like, "Everyone is so happy.

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, this would be a great plac
for something

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:18.905 size:75% position:38% line:92%
horrific to happen."

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, so you think about i
in those terms.

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every time everybody is
really happy, I'm like, "Hmm."

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And do you think the people
around you know that?

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:25.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
That, like,
when they're with you

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:27.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
and things are going
really well, they're like,

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:29.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Uh-oh, somebody's
going to make a movie

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
about something awful
happening here"?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll look for a pencil
or something.

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:34.020 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"What did you say?"

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'll just say,
"Hold on one second.

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:38.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
